# 18. Bug Fixing and Issue Resolution

- Identify the actual root cause before modifying code.
- Do not apply temporary workarounds without understanding the issue.
- Fix the underlying problem rather than hiding the symptoms.
- Check related components, APIs, services, and database operations.
- Avoid introducing new bugs while fixing existing ones.
- Review related modules for side effects.
- Reproduce issues before fixing them whenever possible.
- Verify the fix with appropriate tests.
- Remove temporary debugging code.
- Document important fixes.
- Maintain existing business logic unless a change is explicitly required.

